# Backup + Deploy workflow

When the user asks to **BACKUP** and **DEPLOY** (any casing / Greek/English mix like «KANE BACKUP KAI DEPLOY»):

1. **Filesystem backup first** — run:

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "c:\SportSuite360\scripts\backup-project.ps1"
```

This writes a timestamped ZIP to `C:\SPORTSUITE360_BACKUP\SportSuite360_yyyy-MM-dd_HH-mm-ss.zip` (folder is created if missing). Report the ZIP path to the user.

2. **Git backup commit** — stage relevant project changes and commit with message style:

`Backup: <short summary of what changed>.`

Follow the repo git safety rules (no force push, no amend unless allowed, no secrets).

3. **Deploy** — run production deploy:

```powershell
npx vercel --prod --yes
```

Working directory: `c:\SportSuite360`. Report the production URL (`https://sportsuite360.vercel.app`).

Do **not** skip the ZIP step when the user asks for backup + deploy together.
